{{also|électrolyte}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|electrolysis}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|/ɨˈlɛk.tɹɵˌlaɪt/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|chemistry}} A [[substance]] that, in [[solution]] or when [[molten]], [[ionize]]s and [[conduct]]s [[electricity]].
# {{lb|en|physiology}} Any of the various [[ion]]s (such as [[sodium]] or [[chloride]]) that [[regulate]] the [[electric charge]] on [[cell]]s and the [[flow]] of [[water]] across their [[membrane]]s.

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|electrolytic}}

